      en: ["In Sumerian inscriptions, Jabal al-Bishri was known as the 'Mountain of the Amorites'.", "The massif reaches an average elevation of about 800 meters above sea level.", "The highland area covers nearly 5,000 square kilometers of central Syria.", "The region is home to significant natural bitumen and natural gas deposits.", "Archaeologists have found evidence of settlements dating back to the Natufian culture.", "The area remains a key seasonal grazing ground for Bedouin sheep and camel herds."],
